    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/en/job/503315/commercial-projects-manager-property-and-assets": {
      "title": "Jobs and Careers",
      "description": "Current Vacancies - Jobs and Careers | University of Tasmania Close Home Study with us Uni life Our research For community & partners About us Staff portal Student portal MyLO eStudent Search Close How can we help you? Search Back to Working at the University Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Home About us Working at the University Current job opportunities Applicant login Subscribe Search e.g. “Marketing”, “IMAS”, “Research” Filter results Work type Full time 1 Locations Hobart 1 Categories Professional Infrastructure & Property 1 Commercial Projects Manager, Property and Assets Apply now Job no: 503315 Work type: Full time Location: Hobart Categories: Infrastructure & Property Manage commercialisation initiatives from concept through to implementation Relocation allowance considered for the right candidate Full time, ongoing role based in Hobart The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. About the opportunity As Commercial Projects Manager, Property and Assets, you will lead the identification, development and delivery of strategic commercial projects across the University's property and asset portfolio. Working across all campuses, you will play a key role in maximising the value, utilisation and commercial performance of University assets while supporting long-term institutional objectives. You will be responsible for managing commercialisation initiatives from concept through to implementation, including opportunity identification, feasibility analysis, business case development, deal structuring, negotiation and project delivery. Drawing on strong commercial and financial expertise, you will provide advice on commercial, financial, contractual and property matters, ensuring projects deliver sustainable value and revenue outcomes. The role requires extensive engagement with internal and external stakeholders, including faculty and professional staff, students, industry partners, consultants and tenants. You will build strong relationships, understand evolving space and asset requirements, align projects with broader University priorities and effectively manage stakeholder interests throughout the project lifecycle. What you’ll do: Lead complex commercial property and asset projects from opportunity identification through business case development, approval, negotiation and implementation, coordinating multidisciplinary teams, consultants and external partners. Deliver high-quality commercial and financial analysis, including investment and divestment activities, while managing project transactions and ensuring sound commercial outcomes Develop and maintain a detailed understanding of the University's property and asset portfolio, using space utilisation and allocation analysis to support strategic decision-making. Build strong relationships with internal and external stakeholders to understand strategic priorities, future space requirements and emerging issues, ensuring effective communication and collaboration. Prepare reports, presentations and governance papers, maintain accurate records, and proactively identify and mitigate risks to ensure compliance with relevant legislation, policies and standards. ­ What we’re looking for: A degree in a relevant discipline and experience in property management, or an equivalent combination of relevant experience, education and training Significant experience in commercial project management. Strong knowledge of relevant regulations, codes, and best practices. Excellent analytical, organisational and problem-solving skills, with the ability to identify commercial opportunities and undertake financial modelling. Strong negotiation and contract management abilities with the ability to effectively oversee project transactions Proficiency in relevant software and systems for financial analysis, project planning, contract management and reporting. Salary details Appointment to this role will be at HEO 9 and will have a total remuneration package of up to $160,613 comprising base salary within the range of $130,242 to $137,276 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply To apply online, please provide your CV and 1-2-page cover letter outlining your interest in the role, skills, capabilities and experience.  You do not need to separately address the success profile. For further information about this position, please contact Brendan Parnell, Director Property Strategy on Brendan.Parnell@utas.edu.au or 03 62265297. Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description Below for full details. Position Description - 503315 - Commercial Projects Manager, Property and Assets.pdf Applications close Wednesday, 16 September 2026, 11.55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Advertised: 02 Sep 2026 Tasmania Standard Time Applications close: 16 Sep 2026 Tasmania Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Commercial Projects Manager, Property and Assets Hobart 16 Sep 2026 Lead strategic commercial property and asset initiatives that maximise the value, utilisation and performance of the University's portfolio. Expression of interest Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Expression of Interest Are you an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person looking for a dynamic employment opportunity that allows you to contribute and make a difference in your community? Current Opportunities Position Location Closes Commercial Projects Manager, Property and Assets Hobart 16 Sep 2026 Lead strategic commercial property and asset initiatives that maximise the value, utilisation and performance of the University's portfolio. Powered by PageUp Authorised by the Director of Marketing. © 2025 University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Copyright statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility"
