    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/en/job/503008/lecturer-exercise-science": {
      "title": "Jobs and Careers",
      "description": "Current Vacancies - Jobs and Careers | University of Tasmania Close Home Study with us Uni life Our research For community & partners About us Staff portal Student portal MyLO eStudent Search Close How can we help you? Search Back to Working at the University Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Home About us Working at the University Current job opportunities Applicant login Subscribe Search e.g. “Marketing”, “IMAS”, “Research” Filter results Work type Full time 1 Locations Launceston 1 Categories Academic Balanced Research/Teaching 1 Lecturer - Exercise Science Apply now Job no: 503008 Work type: Full time Location: Launceston Categories: Balanced Research/Teaching Contribute to excellence in Exercise and Sports Science teaching, research and academia Develop and deliver curriculum in partnership with industry, health and high-performance sectors Full time, ongoing role based in Launceston About the opportunity We are seeking to appoint a Lecturer in Exercise and Sports Sciences to join the multidisciplinary School of Health Sciences. As part of UTAS Health, the School of Health Sciences is strongly partnered with other Health Academic Units including the Tasmanian School of Medicine, School of Psychological Sciences, School of Pharmacy and Pharmacology, School of Nursing, School of Paramedicine, Wicking Dementia Research and Education Centre, and the Menzies Institute for Medical Research. What you’ll do: Make an effective and sustained contribution to the University in achieving its strategic objectives and fulfilling its operational responsibilities. Undertake high-quality scholarly coursework teaching, including unit coordination, development of teaching materials, delivery of teaching and student assessment, including the utilisation of emerging technologies and simulation-based education, and develop leadership capabilities in learning and teaching. Design and facilitate high-quality learning experiences that align with and support the University of Tasmania Graduate Capability Framework, embedding relevant graduate capabilities within curriculum design, delivery, assessment and student learning. As part of a team and with increasing independence, undertake high-quality research in areas of priority, contribute to securing external competitive and other funding, publish research findings, and contribute to the supervision of research higher degree students, in line with the University's research performance expectations for Level B. Develop and maintain productive and effective links within the University and externally with the discipline, profession, industry and community stakeholders. Undertake other duties as assigned by the supervisor.­ What we’re looking for: Demonstrated experience in university-level curriculum development using flexible and innovative learning and teaching approaches, including practical demonstration, simulation-based education, blended delivery and digital technologies. Experience delivering high-quality coursework learning and teaching, including unit coordination, assessment design, quality assurance activities and continuous improvement processes aligned with course learning outcomes. Demonstrated expertise in motor learning and control, biomechanics, exercise physiology, healthspan and behaviour change, exercise assessment and screening, and/or exercise programming. Expertise in other areas such as sport and exercise psychology, health promotion, growth and development, and functional anatomy is desirable. Demonstrated capacity to embed Systems Thinking and Analysis, Adaptive Professional Excellence, Transformative Change Agency for Holistic Sustainability, Creative Innovation and Cultural Expression, and Relational Intelligence and Personal Agency into learning experiences. A growing record of research achievement and an emerging national profile in health and human performance, demonstrated through quality publications, conference presentations, contributions to externally funded research, and the translation of evidence into practice and/or curriculum. Evidence of highly developed interpersonal, communication and organisational skills, including the ability to work collaboratively within multidisciplinary academic teams. Experience contributing to productive relationships within the University and with discipline, professional, industry and community stakeholders at local and national levels. Salary details Appointment to this role will be at Academic Level B and will have a total remuneration package of up to $155,885 comprising base salary within the range of $114,766 to $133,235 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply To apply online, please provide your CV and 1-2-page cover letter outlining your interest in the role, skills, capabilities and experience. In your CV or in an accompanying document, please provide evidence to support your experience and capacity to address the following: Demonstrated experience in university-level curriculum development using flexible and innovative learning and teaching approaches, including practical demonstration, simulation-based education, blended delivery and digital technologies. Experience delivering high-quality coursework learning and teaching, including unit coordination, assessment design, quality assurance activities and continuous improvement processes aligned with course learning outcomes. Demonstrated expertise in motor learning and control, biomechanics, exercise physiology, healthspan and behaviour change, exercise assessment and screening, and/or exercise programming. Expertise in other areas such as sport and exercise psychology, health promotion, growth and development, and functional anatomy is desirable. A growing record of research achievement and an emerging national profile in health and human performance, demonstrated through quality publications, conference presentations, contributions to externally funded research, and the translation of evidence into practice and/or curriculum. Evidence of highly developed interpersonal, communication and organisational skills, including the ability to work collaboratively within multidisciplinary academic teams. Applicants are encouraged to contact Associate Professor Deb Pascoe, School of Health Sciences (deborah.pascoe@utas.edu.au ) for further information about this position. Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description Below for full details. Position Description - 503008 - Lecturer - Exercise Science.pdf Applications close Sunday, 6 September 2026, 11.55pm The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Advertised: 21 Aug 2026 Tasmania Standard Time Applications close: 06 Sep 2026 Tasmania Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Lecturer - Exercise Science Launceston 6 Sep 2026 The School of Health Sciences are seeking a Lecturer in Exercise Science to join its team! Expression of interest Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Expression of Interest Are you an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person looking for a dynamic employment opportunity that allows you to contribute and make a difference in your community? Current Opportunities Position Location Closes Lecturer - Exercise Science Launceston 6 Sep 2026 The School of Health Sciences are seeking a Lecturer in Exercise Science to join its team! Powered by PageUp Authorised by the Director of Marketing. © 2025 University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Copyright statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility"
