    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/en/job/504039/senior-farm-hand": {
      "title": "Jobs and Careers",
      "description": "Current Vacancies - Jobs and Careers | University of Tasmania Close Home Study with us Uni life Our research For community & partners About us Staff portal Student portal MyLO eStudent Search Close How can we help you? Search Back to Working at the University Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Home About us Working at the University Current job opportunities Applicant login Subscribe Search e.g. “Marketing”, “IMAS”, “Research” Filter results Work type Full time 1 Locations Burnie 1 Categories Professional Farming, Animals and Conservation 1 Senior Farm Hand Apply now Job no: 504039 Work type: Full time Location: Burnie Categories: Farming, Animals and Conservation Operate and monitor farm machinery in line with safe work policies and procedures Ensure livestock welfare plans are implemented appropriately Full time, Ongoing role based at the Elliot Research Station (Burnie) The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. About the opportunity The Tasmanian Institute of Agriculture Dairy Research Facility (TDRF) is a 220-hectare farm running a herd of approximately 350 milking cows. The facilities include a state-of-the-art 50 bail rotary dairy with individual cow milk monitoring, walk over weigh scales, body condition score unit and other advanced technologies to support TIA’s research programs. The TDRF hosts research, development and extension activities provided through the TIA Livestock Production Centre’s Research Development and Extension (RD&E) programs. The Senior Farm Hand will support the day-to-day operation of the TDRF including milk harvesting operations, feeding stock, attending to calving and animal health issues and provide guidance and training to team members on these operations. The position will also operate a range of farm machinery including broadacre spraying and apply reproduction practices as set out by a vet program. The Senior Farm Hand will operate in line with industry best practice and regularly engage with researchers, technical staff, farmers and visitors to the TDRF to support operations What you’ll do: Operate and troubleshoot milking plant and equipment, monitor and ensure cleanliness of milk plant, and ensure team members are operating plant and equipment safely and effectively. Operate and monitor all farm machinery that includes haymaking and GPS for spreading and spraying, assess risks and undertake preventative plant and equipment maintenance. Ensure the safe preparation, application (through broadacre and spot spraying) and storage of agrichemicals and fertiliser. Apply reproduction practices as set out by a vet program including identifying reproduction readiness, performing hormone injections and preparing for artificial insemination. Ensure livestock treatment plans are implemented appropriately and ensure animal welfare is appropriately managed through completion of health checks. ­ What we’re looking for: Experience working on a farm with dairy production. Relevant Certificate in Dairy Production or similar field. Advanced knowledge of principles of a pasture based dairy farming operation. Experience operating farm machinery and equipment. Demonstrated ability to work independently and as part of a team. Good organisational skills and record keeping skills. Salary details Appointment to this role will be at Farm and Livestock Hand Level (FLH5) and will have a total remuneration package of up to $84,397 comprising base salary within the range of $65,113 to $72,134 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply To apply online, please provide your CV and 1-2-page cover letter outlining your interest in the role, skills, capabilities and experience.  You do not need to separately address the success profile. For further information about this position, please contact Andrew Marshall, Dairy Research Farm Manager on AA.Marshall@utas.edu.au or 0362260080. Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description Below for full details. Position Description - 504039 - Senior Farm Hand.pdf Applications close Sunday, 6 September 2026, 11.55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Advertised: 21 Aug 2026 Tasmania Standard Time Applications close: 06 Sep 2026 Tasmania Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Senior Farm Hand Burnie 6 Sep 2026 Support the day-to-day operations of the Tasmanian Institute of Agriculture’s 220-hectare Dairy Research Facility Expression of interest Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Expression of Interest Are you an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person looking for a dynamic employment opportunity that allows you to contribute and make a difference in your community? Current Opportunities Position Location Closes Senior Farm Hand Burnie 6 Sep 2026 Support the day-to-day operations of the Tasmanian Institute of Agriculture’s 220-hectare Dairy Research Facility Powered by PageUp Authorised by the Director of Marketing. © 2025 University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Copyright statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility"
