    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/en/job/504156/systems-manager-simulations": {
      "title": "Current Vacancies - Jobs and Careers",
      "description": "Current Vacancies - Jobs and Careers | University of Tasmania Close Home Study with us Uni life Our research For community & partners About us Staff portal Student portal MyLO eStudent Search Close How can we help you? Search Back to Working at the University Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Home About us Working at the University Current job opportunities Applicant login Subscribe Search e.g. “Marketing”, “IMAS”, “Research” Filter results Work type Full time 1 Locations Launceston 1 Categories Professional Information Technology 1 Management 1 Systems Manager, Simulations Apply now Job no: 504156 Work type: Full time Location: Launceston Categories: Management, Information Technology The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Lead and support the technology that powers world-class maritime simulation facilities Contribute to nationally recognised training, research and industry engagement activities Full time, Ongoing role based at AMC, Launceston About the opportunity The Systems Manager, Simulations provides specialist technical expertise supporting the operation, reliability, security and continuous improvement of the Centre for Maritime Simulations' technology infrastructure and simulation systems. The position is responsible for administering and maintaining complex simulation environments, including Linux and Windows operating systems, networking infrastructure, server and storage platforms, simulation hardware, visual systems, and specialised maritime simulation software. The role ensures simulation facilities remain operationally ready to support teaching, research, commercial activities and industry engagement across a diverse range of maritime simulation technologies. Working within a highly specialised maritime simulation environment, the Systems Manager, Simulations provides expert technical support and advice, contributes to infrastructure planning and capability development, develops operational procedures and technical documentation, and works collaboratively with staff, clients, industry partners and technology vendors to maximise the effectiveness, reliability and availability of the University's simulation capability. The role requires advanced technical expertise, initiative, sound judgement and a strong commitment to operational excellence and continuous improvement. You will join a collaborative and supportive team that values diverse perspectives and provides opportunities for ongoing learning, professional growth and meaningful contribution to teaching and research excellence. What you’ll do: Maintain and optimise the technology that powers our world-class maritime simulation facilities. Administer and support Linux, Windows, virtualised and networked systems, ensuring reliable day-to-day operations. Prepare, configure and troubleshoot simulation environments supporting teaching, research and industry training activities. Drive best-practice system governance through technical documentation, quality assurance and continuous improvement initiatives. Partner with staff, students, industry clients and technology vendors to deliver innovative, high-performing simulation services. What we’re looking for: Demonstrated experience administering and supporting Linux and Windows operating systems in complex technical environments. Proven experience managing servers, storage, networking and virtualised infrastructure. Strong troubleshooting and problem-solving skills, with the ability to maintain and optimise specialised hardware and software systems. Experience supporting mission-critical environments where reliability, availability and system performance are essential. Excellent communication skills, with the ability to work effectively with technical and non-technical stakeholders. Ability to work independently, exercise sound judgement and resolve complex technical issues. Experience evaluating, implementing or supporting emerging technologies, including AI-enabled tools, automation platforms and intelligent information systems, to improve operational efficiency and service delivery. Salary details Appointment to this role will be at HEO 6 and will have a total remuneration package of up to $116,872 comprising base salary within the range of $92,120 to $99,891 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply To apply online, please provide your CV and 1-2-page cover letter outlining your interest in the role, skills, capabilities and experience.  You do not need to separately address the success profile. For further information about this position, please contact Damien Freeman, Facility Manager - Centre for Maritime Simulations, D.Freeman@utas.edu.au Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description Below for full details. Position-Description-CMS Systems Manager - 504156.pdf Applications close Sunday, 27 September 2026, 11.55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Advertised: 11 Sep 2026 Tasmania Standard Time Applications close: 27 Sep 2026 Tasmania Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Systems Manager, Simulations Launceston 27 Sep 2026 Keep the technology behind Australia's leading maritime simulators running at peak performance, supporting world-class training, research and industry engagement Expression of interest Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Expression of Interest Are you an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person looking for a dynamic employment opportunity that allows you to contribute and make a difference in your community? Current Opportunities Position Location Closes Systems Manager, Simulations Launceston 27 Sep 2026 Keep the technology behind Australia's leading maritime simulators running at peak performance, supporting world-class training, research and industry engagement Powered by PageUp Authorised by the Director of Marketing. © 2025 University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Copyright statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility"
