    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/en/job/504178/lecturersenior-lecturer-in-outdoor-and-environmental-education": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Outdoor and Environmental Education",
      "description": "Current Vacancies - Jobs and Careers | University of Tasmania Close Home Study with us Uni life Our research For community & partners About us Staff portal Student portal MyLO eStudent Search Close How can we help you? Search Back to Working at the University Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Home About us Working at the University Current job opportunities Applicant login Subscribe Search e.g. “Marketing”, “IMAS”, “Research” Filter results Work type Full time 1 Locations Hobart 1 Categories Academic Balanced Research/Teaching 1 Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Outdoor and Environmental Education Apply now Job no: 504178 Work type: Full time Location: Hobart Categories: Balanced Research/Teaching The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Deliver high-quality Outdoor and Environmental Education programs across online and face-to-face settings, supporting curriculum innovation and teacher education Collaborate with schools, government, and community organisations to strengthen educational outcomes, teacher capability, and community wellbeing Full time, ongoing position based in Hobart, Tasmania About the opportunity The Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Outdoor and Environmental Education is an innovative educator-researcher who contributes to the design, development and delivery of high-quality teaching and curriculum development, while conducting impactful research aligned with the University of Tasmania mission. The successful applicant may deliver programs in a flexible, fully online and face to face models; and contribute to excellence in teacher education, research and engagement. The successful candidate will have a profile that allows them to teach across a range of areas within the school, including in Outdoor and Environmental Education, and will have a strong commitment to the crucial role of education to enable individuals and communities to flourish. Experience teaching within Initial Teacher Education programs will be highly regarded. What you’ll do: Develop, coordinate and deliver high-quality undergraduate and postgraduate teaching in Education and related areas within ITE and non-ITE programs Contribute to innovative curriculum design and continuous improvement of learning experiences that support student success and graduate readiness Coordinate and provide academic leadership to support teaching staff where required. Make an effective and sustained contribution to the University in achieving its strategic objectives and fulfilling its operational responsibilities. Undertake high-quality research of national and increasingly of international standing, seek external competitive and other funding, publish research findings and contribute to the successful supervision of research higher degree students, in order to meet and regularly exceed the University’s research performance expectations for Level B or Level C. Contribute to the development and maintenance of productive partnerships and effective relationships within the University and the discipline, relevant interdisciplinary domains, profession, industry and/or wider community at local and national levels. ­ What we’re looking for: Academic level B A PhD or equivalent in a relevant field. Demonstrated experience in leading and delivering high-quality teaching and learning in at least two of the following environments: bush, alpine, river, coastal, and / or rock. Demonstrated record of, and ongoing commitment to, research that has achieved national recognition and made worthwhile contributions to the field of Outdoor and Environmental Education, demonstrated by a record of quality publications, presentations at conferences and preferably success in securing external competitive and other funding. Demonstrated experience in delivering and supporting high-quality University level teaching and learning in Outdoor & Environmental Education Experience designing, developing or contributing to curriculum and assessment aligned with learning outcomes A record of contributing to building and maintaining effective and productive links locally and nationally with the discipline, profession, industry and wider community. Academic level C A PhD or equivalent in a relevant field. Demonstrated experience in leading and delivering high-quality teaching and learning at least two of bush, alpine, river, coastal, and / or rock environments A strong record in, and continuing commitment to, research that has achieved national and preferably international recognition and made notable contributions to the field of Outdoor and Environmental Education, demonstrated by a record of high-quality publications, presentations at conferences and success in securing external competitive and other funding. A demonstrated record of successful HDR supervision and research leadership, including contribution to research capacity building. Demonstrated experience in delivering and supporting high-quality University-level teaching and learning in Outdoor & Environmental Education Demonstrated experience designing or contributing to curriculum and assessment aligned with learning outcomes A record of contributing to building and maintaining effective and productive links locally and nationally with the discipline, profession, industry and wider community. Salary details Academic Level B and will have a total remuneration package of up to $155,885 comprising base salary within the range of $114,766 to $133,235 plus 17% superannuation. Academic Level C and will have a total remuneration package of up to $184,076 comprising base salary within the range of $138,536 to $157,330 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply To apply online, please provide the following supporting documentation: Resume Cover letter outlining your suitability and motivation for the role Your responses to the Role Specific Skills, Knowledge and Experience from the Position Description below For further information about this position, please contact Marcus Morse, Associate Professor in Outdoor and Environmental Education, marcus.morse@utas.edu.au Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description Below for full details. Position Description - 50417 - Lecturer in Outdoor and Environmental Education.pdf Position Description - 50417 - Senior Lecturer in Outdoor and Environmental Education.pdf Applications close Sunday, 4 October 2026, 11.55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of Advertised: 11 Sep 2026 Tasmania Standard Time Applications close: 04 Oct 2026 Tasmania Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Outdoor and Environmental Education Hobart 4 Oct 2026 Exciting opportunity for an innovative Outdoor and Environmental Educator with a passion for positively impacting the wellbeing and educational attainment of all Tasmanians Expression of interest Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Expression of Interest Are you an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person looking for a dynamic employment opportunity that allows you to contribute and make a difference in your community? Current Opportunities Position Location Closes Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Outdoor and Environmental Education Hobart 4 Oct 2026 Exciting opportunity for an innovative Outdoor and Environmental Educator with a passion for positively impacting the wellbeing and educational attainment of all Tasmanians Powered by PageUp Authorised by the Director of Marketing. © 2025 University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Copyright statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility"
    },
    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/en/job/504190/lecturersenior-lecturer-in-education": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Education",
      "description": "Current Vacancies - Jobs and Careers | University of Tasmania Close Home Study with us Uni life Our research For community & partners About us Staff portal Student portal MyLO eStudent Search Close How can we help you? Search Back to Working at the University Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Home About us Working at the University Current job opportunities Applicant login Subscribe Search e.g. “Marketing”, “IMAS”, “Research” Filter results Work type Full time 1 Locations Burnie 1 Hobart 1 Launceston 1 Categories Academic Teaching Intensive 1 Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Education Apply now Job no: 504190 Work type: Full time Location: Hobart, Launceston, Burnie Categories: Teaching Intensive The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Initial Teacher Education with expertise in Cognitive Science, Psychology and the Science of Learning Enjoy flexible working arrangements, generous superannuation and extensive leave provisions Full time, Ongoing role located in Hobart, Launceston or Burnie. Flexible work arrangements available About the opportunity Shape tomorrow's teachers through the science of learning. The School of Education is seeking passionate and innovative educators to join our team as either a Lecturer or Senior Lecturer in Education. Working within Initial Teacher Education, you will contribute to teaching, research and engagement activities with a focus on cognitive science, educational psychology and evidence-based teaching practices. Whether you are an emerging academic building your research profile or an established scholar with a record of academic leadership, this is an opportunity to influence how future teachers learn, teach and make a lasting impact in classrooms and communities. What you’ll do: Shape the next generation of teachers through high-quality teaching and mentorship. Deliver engaging learning experiences informed by cognitive science and evidence-based practice. Contribute to research that advances understanding of how students learn. Build strong partnerships with schools, communities and the broader education sector. Supervise and support research students. Collaborate with colleagues to drive excellence in teacher education. About you: Lecturer (Level B) Emerging or established teaching and research profile in education, cognitive science, psychology or a related field. Demonstrated capacity to contribute to research and teaching excellence. Interest in building research impact, grant success and academic leadership. S enior Lecturer (Level C) Established teaching and research profile with a record of academic leadership. Demonstrated success in research funding and supervision of higher degree research students. Capacity to teach across cognitive science and broader areas of teacher education. National, and ideally international, recognition in the field. Salary details Appointment to this role will be at Academic Level B or C and will have a total remuneration package of up to $184,076 comprising base salary within the range of $114,766 to $157,330 plus 17% superannuation. Relocation support may be available to the successful candidate, helping make a move to Tasmania as seamless as possible. How to Apply To apply online, please provide the following supporting documentation: Resume Cover letter outlining your suitability and motivation for the role Your responses to the success criteria from the Position Description below For further information about this position, please contact Professor Robyn Cox, Professor in Education, Robyn.Cox@utas.edu.au Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description Below for full details. Position Description - 504190 - Lecturer in Education.pdf Position Description - 504190 - Senior Lecturer in Education.pdf Applications close Sunday, 4 October 2026, 11.55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Advertised: 11 Sep 2026 Tasmania Standard Time Applications close: 04 Oct 2026 Tasmania Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Education Hobart, Launceston, Burnie 4 Oct 2026 Bring the science of learning to life and influence the next generation of teachers from any of our Tasmanian campuses Expression of interest Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Expression of Interest Are you an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person looking for a dynamic employment opportunity that allows you to contribute and make a difference in your community? Current Opportunities Position Location Closes Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Education Hobart, Launceston, Burnie 4 Oct 2026 Bring the science of learning to life and influence the next generation of teachers from any of our Tasmanian campuses Powered by PageUp Authorised by the Director of Marketing. © 2025 University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Copyright statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility"
