    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/en/job/504191/associate-lecturerlecturer-in-outdoor-environmental-education": {
      "title": "Associate Lecturer/Lecturer in Outdoor & Environmental Education",
      "description": "Current Vacancies - Jobs and Careers | University of Tasmania Close Home Study with us Uni life Our research For community & partners About us Staff portal Student portal MyLO eStudent Search Close How can we help you? Search Back to Working at the University Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Home About us Working at the University Current job opportunities Applicant login Subscribe Search e.g. “Marketing”, “IMAS”, “Research” Filter results Work type Full time 1 Locations Hobart 1 Categories Academic Teaching Focused 1 Associate Lecturer/Lecturer in Outdoor & Environmental Education Apply now Job no: 504191 Work type: Full time Location: Hobart Categories: Teaching Focused The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Deliver high-quality teaching and curriculum development in Outdoor and Environmental Education across flexible online and face-to-face learning environments, while contributing to excellence in teacher education and research. Collaborate with schools, education providers and community organisations to build capability across Tasmania's education system and drive positive change in educational outcomes and wellbeing. Full time, ongoing position located in Hobart About the opportunity The Associate Lecturer/Lecturer in Outdoor and Environmental Education is an innovative educator-researcher who will contribute to high-quality teaching, curriculum development and impactful research aligned with the University of Tasmania’s mission. The role involves delivering programs across online and face-to-face modes, teaching within Outdoor and Environmental Education and related areas, and supporting excellence in teacher education, research and engagement. The successful candidate will be committed to the role of education in helping individuals and communities flourish, with experience in Initial Teacher Education highly regarded. What you’ll do: Contribute to the development and delivery of high-quality undergraduate and postgraduate teaching in Education and related areas within ITE and non-ITE programs for Level A. Develop, coordinate and deliver high-quality undergraduate and postgraduate teaching in Education and related areas within ITE and non-ITE programs for Level B. Contribute to innovative curriculum design and continuous improvement of learning experiences that support student success and graduate readiness. Coordinate and provide academic leadership to support teaching staff where required. Undertake high-quality research/scholarly activities under limited supervision either independently or as a member of a team, publish research findings as sole author or in collaboration, to meet and regularly exceed the University’s research performance expectations for Level A. Undertake high-quality research of national and increasingly of international standing, to meet and regularly exceed the University’s research performance expectations for Level B. ­Make an effective and sustained contribution to the University in achieving its strategic objectives and fulfilling its operational responsibilities. What we’re looking for: A four-year tertiary qualification in a relevant field and/or equivalent qualifications and/or professional experience for level A. A PhD or equivalent in a relevant field for Level B. Demonstrated experience in supporting  and delivering high-quality teaching and learning at least two of bush, alpine, river, coastal, and / or rock environments for Level A. Demonstrated experience in leading and delivering high-quality teaching and learning in at least two of the following environments: bush, alpine, river, coastal, and / or rock for Level B. A demonstrated ability and understanding of research in the field of Outdoor and Environmental Education, demonstrated by a strong academic record for Level A. Demonstrated record of, and ongoing commitment to, research and writing that has achieved national recognition and made worthwhile contributions to the field of Outdoor and Environmental Education for Level B. Demonstrated experience in delivering and supporting high-quality University level teaching and learning in Outdoor & Environmental Education for Level A. Demonstrated experience in delivering and supporting high-quality University level teaching and learning in Outdoor & Environmental Education for Level B. Salary details Appointment to this role will be at either Academic Level A or Academic Level B and will have a total remuneration package of up to $155,885 comprising base salary within the range of $83,198 to $133,235 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply To apply online, please provide the following supporting documentation: CV Cover letter outlining your suitability and motivation for the role (1 page) Your responses to the success criteria from the Position Description below (Maximum 3 pages) Please respond to either Level A or Level B For further information about this position, please contact Marcus Morse, Associate Professor in Outdoor and Environmental Education, Marcus.Morse@utas.edu.au or 0439097754 Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description Below for full details. Position Description - Associate Lecturer in Outdoor & Environmental Education.pdf (Level A). Position Description - Lecturer in Outdoor & Environmental Education.pdf (Level B). Applications close Sunday, 4 October 2026, 11.55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Advertised: 11 Sep 2026 Tasmania Standard Time Applications close: 04 Oct 2026 Tasmania Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Associate Lecturer/Lecturer in Outdoor & Environmental Education Hobart 4 Oct 2026 Shape the future of education in Tasmania by inspiring the next generation of learners through innovative teaching, impactful research, and meaningful partnerships across the education sector. Expression of interest Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Expression of Interest Are you an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person looking for a dynamic employment opportunity that allows you to contribute and make a difference in your community? Current Opportunities Position Location Closes Associate Lecturer/Lecturer in Outdoor & Environmental Education Hobart 4 Oct 2026 Shape the future of education in Tasmania by inspiring the next generation of learners through innovative teaching, impactful research, and meaningful partnerships across the education sector. Powered by PageUp Authorised by the Director of Marketing. © 2025 University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Copyright statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility"
    },
    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/en/job/504223/change2teaching-education-teaching-practitioner": {
      "title": "Change2Teaching - Education Teaching Practitioner",
      "description": "Current Vacancies - Jobs and Careers | University of Tasmania Close Home Study with us Uni life Our research For community & partners About us Staff portal Student portal MyLO eStudent Search Close How can we help you? Search Back to Working at the University Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Home About us Working at the University Current job opportunities Applicant login Subscribe Search e.g. “Marketing”, “IMAS”, “Research” Filter results Work type Part time 1 Locations Burnie 1 Hobart 1 Categories Academic Teaching Focused 1 Change2Teaching - Education Teaching Practitioner Apply now Job no: 504223 Work type: Part time Location: Hobart, Burnie Categories: Teaching Focused The University of Tasmania acknowledges the palawa/pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Use your teaching expertise to create inclusive and equitable learning environments Shape the next generation of teachers through contemporary, practice-focused education Two positions available to start in January 2027, part-time (0.6–0.8 FTE), on a two-year fixed-term basis in Hobart and Burnie About the opportunity The Associate Lecturer in Education (Practitioner) is a highly skilled educator who contributes to the design, development and delivery of high-quality, practice-focused curriculum within the Change2Teaching pilot program, the Master of Teaching program, and the School of Education more broadly. This role supports a place-based university vision by delivering contemporary, industry-relevant learning experiences that enhance student outcomes and contribute to the intellectual, social and cultural future of Tasmania. What you’ll do: Contribute to the design and development of units, including preparation of unit outlines and teaching materials. Deliver lectures, tutorials, workshops, consultations and other learning activities. Contribute to the development of student assessment tasks and supporting materials. Assess student work and provide appropriate feedback in line with University standards. Support student academic welfare, including identifying needs and referring students to appropriate services.­ What we’re looking for: A minimum Master level degree in Education with school experience, or an equivalent combination of qualifications and professional experience in education. Demonstrated experience in delivering and supporting high quality teaching and learning. Experience designing or contributing to curriculum and assessment aligned with learning outcomes. Ability to adapt teaching approaches to suit different learning styles and delivery modes. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to collaborate effectively. Salary details Appointment to this role will be at Academic Level A and will have a total remuneration package of up to $125,877 comprising base salary within the range of $83,198 to $107,587 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply To apply online, please provide the following supporting documentation: Resume Cover letter outlining your suitability and motivation for the role Your responses to the success criteria from the Position Description below For further information about this position, please contact Mary Ann Hunter, Associate Professor, MaryAnn.Hunter@utas.edu.au Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description Below for full details. Position Description - 504223 - Change2Teaching - Education Teaching Practitioner.pdf Applications close Sunday, 4 October 2026, 11.55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Advertised: 11 Sep 2026 Tasmania Standard Time Applications close: 04 Oct 2026 Tasmania Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Change2Teaching - Education Teaching Practitioner Hobart, Burnie 4 Oct 2026 Seeking a highly skilled educator for two-year pilot program, Change2Teaching - Education Teaching Practitioner Expression of interest Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Expression of Interest Are you an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person looking for a dynamic employment opportunity that allows you to contribute and make a difference in your community? Current Opportunities Position Location Closes Change2Teaching - Education Teaching Practitioner Hobart, Burnie 4 Oct 2026 Seeking a highly skilled educator for two-year pilot program, Change2Teaching - Education Teaching Practitioner Powered by PageUp Authorised by the Director of Marketing. © 2025 University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Copyright statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility"
