    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/en/job/504208/manager-professional-experience-placement": {
      "title": "Current Vacancies - Jobs and Careers",
      "description": "Current Vacancies - Jobs and Careers | University of Tasmania Close Home Study with us Uni life Our research For community & partners About us Staff portal Student portal MyLO eStudent Search Close How can we help you? Search Back to Working at the University Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Home About us Working at the University Current job opportunities Applicant login Subscribe Search e.g. “Marketing”, “IMAS”, “Research” Filter results Work type Full time 1 Locations Launceston 1 Categories Professional Management 1 Student Services 1 Manager, Professional Experience Placement Apply now Job no: 504208 Work type: Full time Location: Launceston Categories: Management, Student Services The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Bring your passion for education to a role that shapes exceptional placement experiences Lead and inspire a professional team dedicated to enriching student learning and success Full time, ongoing position based at the Rivers Edge Campus, Launceston About the opportunity We are seeking to appoint a Manager, Professional Experience Placement in the School of Education, which is part of the Arts and Society Portfolio . The Manager, Professional Experience Placement supports the Portfolio’s strategic initiative to grow and enhance high-quality placement experiences, which is a key component to support student learning and development within their course. What you’ll do: Manage the day-to-day operations of the Professional Experience administrative team, overseeing the delivery of support across all student placement end-to-end lifecycle activities. Lead and develop the Professional Experience administrative team, establishing a values-based, people-centric environment that supports all staff and students to achieve their best individually and collectively. Effectively mitigate risk by ensuring compliance with UTAS and external policy, including but not limited to, adherence to the UTAS PEP Procedure, management of student and stakeholder compliance, and external accreditation requirements. Provide high level and strategic advice, guidance and recommendations in relation to improvements, changes and new approaches to Professional Experience programs across the Portfolio. Make key and knowledgeable contributions to the design and delivery of strategic and operational plans, policy and procedure in the area of Professional Experience, in consultation with senior academic and professional staff within the Portfoilio and wider University. ­ What we’re looking for: A bachelor’s level qualification with relevant experience or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and/or education/training. Proven team building and team leadership skills, with an ability to work constructively and an ability to lead a continuous improvement culture. Experience with policy interpretation and implementation, including the ongoing review of administrative processes and procedures to ensure they provide a quality approach. Excellent written communication skills including the ability to research and analyse information in order to present data, and write effective reports, plans, submissions and correspondence. Experience supporting University professional experience placement programs an advantage, not essential. Demonstrated high-level interpersonal and verbal communication skills including the ability to clearly consult and liaise with internal and external stakeholders in a professionally and culturally sensitive manner. Salary details Appointment to this role will be at HEO 7 and will have a total remuneration package of up to $130,943 comprising base salary within the range of $101,821 to $111,917 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply To apply online, please provide your CV and 1-2-page cover letter outlining your interest in the role, skills, capabilities and experience.  You do not need to separately address the success profile. For further information about this position, please contact Catherine Chalmers, Business Manager, catherine.chalmers@utas.edu.au or Isobel Starrett, School Coordinator, isobel.starrett@utas.edu.au Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description Below for full details. Position Description 504208 - Manager, Professional Experience Placement.pdf Applications close Sunday, 20 September 2026, 11.55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Advertised: 07 Sep 2026 Tasmania Standard Time Applications close: 20 Sep 2026 Tasmania Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Manager, Professional Experience Placement Launceston 20 Sep 2026 Lead a dynamic team at the University of Tasmania and play a pivotal role in creating placement experiences that empower students to thrive in their future professions Expression of interest Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Expression of Interest Are you an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person looking for a dynamic employment opportunity that allows you to contribute and make a difference in your community? Current Opportunities Position Location Closes Manager, Professional Experience Placement Launceston 20 Sep 2026 Lead a dynamic team at the University of Tasmania and play a pivotal role in creating placement experiences that empower students to thrive in their future professions Powered by PageUp Authorised by the Director of Marketing. © 2025 University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Copyright statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility"
