    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/en/job/503787/head-school-of-health-sciences": {
      "title": "Current Vacancies - Jobs and Careers",
      "description": "Current Vacancies - Jobs and Careers | University of Tasmania Close Home Study with us Uni life Our research For community & partners About us Staff portal Student portal MyLO eStudent Search Close How can we help you? Search Back to Working at the University Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Home About us Working at the University Current job opportunities Applicant login Subscribe Search e.g. “Marketing”, “IMAS”, “Research” Filter results Work type Full time 1 Locations Launceston 1 Categories Academic Balanced Research/Teaching 1 Head, School of Health Sciences Apply now Job no: 503787 Work type: Full time Location: Launceston Categories: Balanced Research/Teaching The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Build impactful partnerships across health services, government, industry and communities to shape Tasmania's future health workforce. Lead a diverse portfolio spanning allied health, exercise and sports science, and laboratory medicine. Foster a high-performing, inclusive and collaborative culture. About the Opportunity We are seeking to appoint an exceptional and inspiring leader as Head of School, Health Sciences, based in Launceston, Tasmania. This is a rare opportunity to lead a School that is making a tangible difference to the health and wellbeing of Tasmanian communities through education, research and partnership. Home to disciplines spanning allied health, exercise and sports science, and laboratory medicine, the School is uniquely positioned at the intersection of community need, workforce development and health innovation. Based within the University's state-of-the-art facilities in Launceston, you will lead a collaborative and interdisciplinary academic community united by a shared purpose: improving lives through better health outcomes. Through deep partnerships with health services, government, industry and community organisations, the School is shaping the next generation of health professionals and helping address Tasmania's most pressing workforce and health challenges. As a key member of the UTAS Health leadership team, you will help realise the University's vision of creating healthier, more connected communities. This is an opportunity to influence the future of Tasmania's health system through education, research and collaboration, strengthening workforce capability and delivering lasting impact for generations to come. About the University The University of Tasmania is a mission-driven institution dedicated to making a difference for Lutruwita/Tasmania and a distinctive contribution from Tasmania to the world. As the sole university on the island, the University is deeply embedded in the social, economic, and environmental fabric of Tasmania, working in close partnership with communities, industry, and government to address key challenges in education, health, productivity, and climate action. The University takes pride in its place-based identity, leveraging Tasmania’s unique geography, culture, and resources to offer world-leading research and education. What We are Looking For We are seeking an accomplished and collaborative leader who is passionate about the role higher education can play in improving health outcomes and building workforce capability. You will bring significant leadership experience within a university, health or allied health setting, along with the ability to inspire high-performing teams and foster a mission-driven culture of excellence, inclusion and innovation. With a strong understanding of the contemporary health landscape, you will be skilled at building strategic partnerships, navigating complexity and balancing academic, operational and financial priorities. Most importantly, you will be a values-led leader who thinks beyond organisational boundaries, embraces collaboration, and is motivated by the opportunity to make a lasting contribution to Tasmania's communities, health system and future workforce. What’s on Offer? As we look toward 2050, we remain committed to fostering excellence, collaboration, and transformative education - preparing graduates to navigate the challenges of a rapidly changing world, and shape its future. While remaining true to our Tasmanian roots, this career defining role will see you significantly contribute to our dedication to making a difference for, and from, Tasmania. In return for your experience, you’ll have access to an array of staff benefits and discounts including: 26 Weeks paid parental leave for primary care givers 17% Superannuation contribution Health and fitness membership options Accommodation and Car Hire discounts Health Insurance and Banking Novated Leasing Generous relocation support to Tasmania How to Apply? If this role is of interest, we look forward to hearing from you. Please provide your up-to-date resume and: A 1-2 page cover letter outlining your motivation for the role at the University of Tasmania A separate response outlining how your skills and experience align with the role specific skills, knowledge and experience in the Position Description Applications close 11.55pm Sunday the 25th of October 2026. Position Description Head of Health Sciences Sept 2026 .pdf For further information about this position, please contact the Talent Acquisition team via email: TalentTeam@utas.edu.au To be eligible for this position, you are required to have Australian citizenship, permanent residence or a current valid visa that allows you to fulfill the requirements of this role. As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police background checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. Advertised: 28 Sep 2026 Tasmania Standard Time Applications close: 25 Oct 2026 Tasmania Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Head, School of Health Sciences Launceston 25 Oct 2026 Lead the strategic direction of the School of Health Sciences, advancing health education, research and workforce impact across Tasmania. Expression of interest Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Expression of Interest Are you an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person looking for a dynamic employment opportunity that allows you to contribute and make a difference in your community? Current Opportunities Position Location Closes Head, School of Health Sciences Launceston 25 Oct 2026 Lead the strategic direction of the School of Health Sciences, advancing health education, research and workforce impact across Tasmania. Powered by PageUp Authorised by the Director of Marketing. © 2025 University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Copyright statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility"
    },
    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/en/job/504174/administration-officer-administrative-services": {
      "title": "Current Vacancies - Jobs and Careers",
      "description": "Current Vacancies - Jobs and Careers | University of Tasmania Close Home Study with us Uni life Our research For community & partners About us Staff portal Student portal MyLO eStudent Search Close How can we help you? Search Back to Working at the University Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Home About us Working at the University Current job opportunities Applicant login Subscribe Search e.g. “Marketing”, “IMAS”, “Research” Filter results Work type Full time 1 Locations Hobart 1 Categories Professional Administration 1 Administration Officer, Administrative Services Apply now Job no: 504174 Work type: Full time Location: Hobart Categories: Administration The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Use your administrative and organisational skills in a varied role across our Arts and Society teams Join a collaborative team where your contribution helps support staff, students and the wider University community Full-time, ongoing role based in Hobart. About the opportunity The Administration Officer centrally supports the activities of the Academic Units within the Arts and Society portfolio by delivering high‑quality, reliable administrative services across a broad range of functions. These include communications, finance, travel, procurement, people and culture processes, research support, facilities and WHS coordination, event assistance, and academic administration. The role ensures smooth day‑to‑day operations by providing efficient, customer‑focused service, and by contributing to consistent, streamlined administrative practices across the portfolio’s schools and disciplines. Success in this role requires the ability to build positive working relationships, collaborate effectively with colleagues, and engage confidently with stakeholders in person, online and by phone. Strong organisational skills, initiative, and the capacity to manage multiple tasks concurrently are essential, alongside competence in utilising administrative systems, including the University’s service management platform (Help Hub). What you’ll do: Provide responsive, customer-focused administrative support to academic and professional staff across Arts and Society. Provide accurate, solutions-focused advice and assistance, applying relevant policies and procedures to support staff enquiries. Contribute to a positive and high‑performing service culture by identifying opportunities for service improvement and developing specialist expertise to lead key processes or initiatives. Support learning and teaching programs, including the coordination of student activities and other key administrative tasks. Assist with internal communications and events, engaging professionally with staff, students and the wider community. Contribute to a positive and high-performing service culture by identifying opportunities to improve processes and service delivery. ­ What we’re looking for: Demonstrated commitment to customer service excellence and the continuous improvement of systems, processes and procedures. Excellent interpersonal, resilience, communication and influencing skills with a positive, ‘can-do’ attitude that enhance an ability to communicate effectively with a broad range of people. Proven ability to work in a collaborative team environment and demonstrated capacity to act independently within established guidelines. Exceptional organisational skills and a demonstrated ability to perform tasks with a high degree of accuracy, with a commitment to maintaining confidentiality, using discretion and sound judgement. Strong attention to detail. A high level of computer literacy, including competence in the Microsoft 365 suite, and experience with other database operations Salary details Appointment to this role will be at HEO 4 and will have a total remuneration package of up to $91,488 comprising base salary within the range of $73,814 to $78,195 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply To apply online, please provide your CV and 1-2-page cover letter outlining your interest in the role, skills, capabilities and experience.  You do not need to separately address the success profile. For further information about this position, please contact Frances Wayman, Manager, Administrative Services, Arts & Society, email - Frances.Wayman@utas.edu.au Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description Below for full details. Position Description - 504174 - Administration Officer.pdf Applications close Sunday, 4 October 2026, 11.55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Advertised: 25 Sep 2026 Tasmania Standard Time Applications close: 04 Oct 2026 Tasmania Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Administration Officer, Administrative Services Hobart 4 Oct 2026 Bring your organisational and people skills to a collaborative team supporting our Arts and Society community Expression of interest Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Expression of Interest Are you an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person looking for a dynamic employment opportunity that allows you to contribute and make a difference in your community? Current Opportunities Position Location Closes Administration Officer, Administrative Services Hobart 4 Oct 2026 Bring your organisational and people skills to a collaborative team supporting our Arts and Society community Powered by PageUp Authorised by the Director of Marketing. © 2025 University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Copyright statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility"
