    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/en/job/504328/director-conservatorium-of-music": {
      "title": "Director, Conservatorium of Music",
      "description": "Current Vacancies - Jobs and Careers | University of Tasmania Close Home Study with us Uni life Our research For community & partners About us Staff portal Student portal MyLO eStudent Search Close How can we help you? Search Back to Working at the University Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Home About us Working at the University Current job opportunities Applicant login Subscribe Search e.g. “Marketing”, “IMAS”, “Research” Filter results Work type Full time 1 Locations Hobart 1 Categories Professional Management 1 Director, Conservatorium of Music Apply now Job no: 504328 Work type: Full time Location: Hobart Categories: Management The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Shape and strengthen music programs, research activity and creative practice. Build impactful partnerships across industry, government, schools and the arts sector. Foster an inclusive, collaborative and high-performing culture that supports staff and student success. About the Opportunity We are seeking to appoint an exceptional and visionary leader as Director of the Conservatorium, a pivotal role within the Arts and Society leadership team. In this role, you will provide strategic, academic and operational leadership, supporting the continued development of the Conservatorium's music programs, research activities and community partnerships. You will lead and support a vibrant music community, fostering a connected, inclusive and high-performing culture where students, staff and industry partners can thrive. Working across the University and with government, arts organisations, schools and community stakeholders, you will strengthen the reach, impact and reputation of the Conservatorium's music programs and creative activities. As a people-centred leader, you will translate strategy into action, champion academic excellence and innovation, and ensure the Conservatorium continues to deliver distinctive and sustainable outcomes that enrich Tasmanian culture, creativity and community. About the University The University of Tasmania is a mission-driven institution dedicated to making a difference for Lutruwita/Tasmania and a distinctive contribution from Tasmania to the world. As the sole university on the island, the University is deeply embedded in the social, economic, and environmental fabric of Tasmania, working in close partnership with communities, industry, and government to address key challenges in education, health, productivity, and climate action. The University takes pride in its place-based identity, leveraging Tasmania’s unique geography, culture, and resources to offer world-leading research and education. What We are Looking For We are seeking a collaborative and strategic leader with a strong background in music and related disciplines. You will bring experience leading academic, artistic or creative teams, along with a clear vision for the future of music education and the ability to cultivate meaningful partnerships across industry, government and the community. With strong financial and operational capability, you will be adept at navigating the higher education environment and advancing the Conservatorium's contribution to teaching, research, creative practice and community engagement. You will combine sound judgement with an inclusive leadership style, inspiring others, building strong connections and fostering a culture of excellence, creativity, innovation and collaboration. What’s on Offer? As we look toward 2050, we remain committed to fostering excellence, collaboration, and transformative education - preparing graduates to navigate the challenges of a rapidly changing world, and shape its future. While remaining true to our Tasmanian roots, this career defining role will see you significantly contribute to our dedication to making a difference for, and from, Tasmania. In return for your experience, you’ll have access to an array of staff benefits and discounts including: 26 Weeks paid parental leave for primary care givers 17% Superannuation contribution Health and fitness membership options Accommodation and Car Hire discounts Health Insurance and Banking Novated Leasing How to Apply? If this role is of interest, we look forward to hearing from you. Please provide your up-to-date resume and: A 1-page cover letter outlining your motivation for the role at the University of Tasmania A separate response of up to 3-pages related to the role specific skills, knowledge and experience in the Position Description For further information about this position, please contact the Talent Acquisition team via email: TalentTeam@utas.edu.au Position Description - Director, Conservatorium of Music.pdf Applications close 11.55pm AEST, Sunday 11th of October. To be eligible for this position, you are required to have Australian citizenship, permanent residence or a current valid visa that allows you to fulfill the requirements of this role. As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police background checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. Advertised: 25 Sep 2026 Tasmania Standard Time Applications close: 11 Oct 2026 Tasmania Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Director, Conservatorium of Music Hobart 11 Oct 2026 Lead the strategic direction of the Conservatorium, advancing music education, research, creative practice and community impact. Expression of interest Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Expression of Interest Are you an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person looking for a dynamic employment opportunity that allows you to contribute and make a difference in your community? Current Opportunities Position Location Closes Director, Conservatorium of Music Hobart 11 Oct 2026 Lead the strategic direction of the Conservatorium, advancing music education, research, creative practice and community impact. Powered by PageUp Authorised by the Director of Marketing. © 2025 University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Copyright statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility"
