    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/en/job/504342/senior-field-fleet-officer": {
      "title": "Senior Field & Fleet Officer",
      "description": "Senior Field & Fleet Officer - Hobart, TAS, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Senior Field & Fleet Officer 504342 Hobart, TAS Full time Closing on: 18 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Manage field operations, fleet assets and safety compliance across diverse scientific disciplines. Support staff and students through operational expertise, training and field-trip coordination. Full Time, Ongoing role, based in Hobart (Sandy Bay Campus) About the opportunity The Senior Field and Fleet Officer is responsible for ensuring the safe, effective, and compliant operation of field activities across the School of Natural Sciences (SNS), providing operational, teaching, and training support to staff and students. The role oversees strategic planning, project and asset management, and compliance with University and legislative Work Health and Safety requirements, while managing a fleet of 12 vehicles, trailers, and associated field and communications equipment that support hundreds of field trips annually. Reporting to the SNS Operations Manager and supported by a direct report (Technical Officer – Field & Fleet), the position serves a diverse school encompassing Biology, Chemistry, Earth Sciences, Mathematics, and Physics, supporting both teaching and research activities that rely on fieldwork and fleet resources. What you’ll do: Manage day-to-day field and fleet operations ensuring effective coordination, safety, and operational efficiency Provide safety management support to staff and students by facilitating fieldwork risk assessments, coordinating inductions and organising further training where required. Contribute to the development and implementation of SNS safety procedures including Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs), Safe Work Procedures (SWPs), Risk Assessments and induction materials. Manage and maintain vehicle, trailer and associated field equipment including oversight of booking systems (e.g. PoolCar) and preparation of accurate monthly billing reports. Coordinate asset use and maintenance, ensuring timely servicing and repair of vehicles, trailers and field equipment ­ What we’re looking for: Combination of extensive relevant work experience and/or education/training. Significant experience in providing technical field support including experience in the development and implementation of risk assessments, safe working practices and standard operating protocols in a changing environment. Strong WHS knowledge and safe work systems management, including strong knowledge of field and driving hazards and managing them. Experience managing a fleet of assets, 4WD vehicles would be advantageous. Demonstrated ability to analyse and solve complex technical and non-technical problems and to adapt rapidly to changing priorities and tasks. Experience with remote area communications and specialised off road vehicles will be advantageous Excellent interpersonal skills, including the ability to communicate effectively with students, professional staff and academic staff at all levels, and external stakeholders, and the ability to work in a flexible and collaborative manner. What’s on Offer? As we look toward 2050, we remain committed to fostering excellence, collaboration, and transformative education - preparing graduates to navigate the challenges of a rapidly changing world, and shape its future. While remaining true to our Tasmanian roots, this career defining role will see you significantly contribute to our dedication to making a difference for, and from, Tasmania. In return for your experience, you’ll have access to an array of staff benefits and discounts including: 26 Weeks paid parental leave for primary care givers 17% Superannuation contribution Health and fitness membership options Accommodation and Car Hire discounts Health Insurance and Banking Novated Leasing Relocation Support Salary details Appointment to this role will be at HEO 6 and will have a total remuneration package of up to $116,872 comprising base salary within the range of $92,120 to $99,891 plus 17% superannuation. Relocation support may be available to the successful candidate, helping make a move to Tasmania as seamless as possible. How to Apply To apply online, please provide your CV and 1-2-page cover letter outlining your motivation for the role and include an overview of how your previous skills & experience aligns to the requirements of the role For further information about this position, please contact Andrea Shadbolt, Business Manager, Andrea.Shadbolt@utas.edu.au Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description Below for full details. Position Description - Senior Field & Fleet Officer.pdf . Applications close Sunday, 18 October 2026, 11.55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Recommended Jobs Executive Director The Underwood Institute for Education Hobart, TAS. Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS Management Lead the Underwood Institute for Education to drive educational impact, partnership and system transformation across Tasmania. Learning & Research Librarian Hobart, TAS. Launceston, TAS Information Technology, Library Make a meaningful impact by empowering students, staff and researchers with inclusive learning and research support that enhances their information literacy and academic success. Senior Lecturer in Nursing Hobart, TAS. Launceston, TAS Teaching Intensive Share your nursing expertise, inspire the next generation and help shape the future of Tasmania’s nursing workforce © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
