    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/jobs/rem-business-partner-hobart-tas-australia-statewide-all-locations-in-tasmania": {
      "title": "REM Business Partner",
      "description": "REM Business Partner - Hobart, TAS, Australia - Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 0:00 Loaded : 0% Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 0:00 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles captions and subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. REM Business Partner 504240 Hobart, TAS Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS Full time Closing on: 11 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Act as a trusted advisor to stakeholders, identifying recruitment, engagement, and marketing opportunities. Drive strategic solutions that enhance student attraction, engagement, and brand positioning while aligning with University priorities. Full time, Fixed-Term (12 months) position located in Hobart. About the opportunity The REM Business Partner operates within assigned stakeholder groups (Academic Units and Divisions) and acts as a trusted advisor, deeply understanding stakeholder priorities and challenges. The role focuses on diagnosing recruitment, engagement, and marketing opportunities then connecting client needs with the right expertise within REM teams. This position ensures initiatives align with the University’s Strategic Plan and delivers data-driven solutions that enhance student attraction, engagement, and brand positioning. What you’ll do: Build strong, influential relationships with stakeholders to anticipate needs and identify opportunities. Diagnose recruitment, engagement, and marketing challenges using data-driven insights and internal and external market intelligence. Provide strategic advice and recommendations, engaging specialist teams to deliver tailored solutions. Lead market analysis and audience segmentation to inform recruitment and engagement strategies. Identify, scope, and oversee major campaigns that support student recruitment and brand objectives. What we’re looking for: Qualifications in Marketing, Communications, Business, or a related discipline, or equivalent relevant experience in these areas or in student recruitment. Expertise in market research, audience insights, and campaign strategy. Ability to analyse and translate data into actionable marketing and recruitment plans. Strategic thinking combined with practical understanding of campaign delivery. Strong stakeholder engagement and relationship management skills. Salary details Appointment to this role will be at HEO 7 and will have a total remuneration package of up to $130,943 comprising base salary within the range of $101,821 to $111,917 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply To apply online, please provide your CV and 1-2-page cover letter outlining your interest in the role, skills, capabilities and experience with reference to the accountabilities and outcomes.  You do not need to separately address the success profile. For further information about this position, please contact Greg Findlay, Director, Marketing, Gregor.Findlay@utas.edu.au or 6220 7857 Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description Below for full details. Position Description - REM Business Partner.pdf . Applications close Sunday, 11 October 2026, 11.55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Back to job search Recommended Jobs Executive Director The Underwood Institute for Education Hobart, TAS. Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS Management Lead the Underwood Institute for Education to drive educational impact, partnership and system transformation across Tasmania. Learning & Research Librarian Hobart, TAS. Launceston, TAS Information Technology, Library Make a meaningful impact by empowering students, staff and researchers with inclusive learning and research support that enhances their information literacy and academic success. Senior Lecturer in Nursing Hobart, TAS. Launceston, TAS Teaching Intensive Share your nursing expertise, inspire the next generation and help shape the future of Tasmania’s nursing workforce © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
