    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/jobs/lecturer-senior-lecturer-in-outdoor-and-environmental-education-hobart-tas-australia": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Outdoor and Environmental Education",
      "description": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Outdoor and Environmental Education - Hobart, TAS, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 0:00 Loaded : 0% Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 0:00 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles captions and subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Outdoor and Environmental Education 504178 Hobart, TAS Full time Closing on: 4 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Deliver high-quality Outdoor and Environmental Education programs across online and face-to-face settings, supporting curriculum innovation and teacher education Collaborate with schools, government, and community organisations to strengthen educational outcomes, teacher capability, and community wellbeing Full time, ongoing position based in Hobart, Tasmania About the opportunity The Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Outdoor and Environmental Education is an innovative educator-researcher who contributes to the design, development and delivery of high-quality teaching and curriculum development, while conducting impactful research aligned with the University of Tasmania mission. The successful applicant may deliver programs in a flexible, fully online and face to face models; and contribute to excellence in teacher education, research and engagement. The successful candidate will have a profile that allows them to teach across a range of areas within the school, including in Outdoor and Environmental Education, and will have a strong commitment to the crucial role of education to enable individuals and communities to flourish. Experience teaching within Initial Teacher Education programs will be highly regarded. What you’ll do: Develop, coordinate and deliver high-quality undergraduate and postgraduate teaching in Education and related areas within ITE and non-ITE programs Contribute to innovative curriculum design and continuous improvement of learning experiences that support student success and graduate readiness Coordinate and provide academic leadership to support teaching staff where required. Make an effective and sustained contribution to the University in achieving its strategic objectives and fulfilling its operational responsibilities. Undertake high-quality research of national and increasingly of international standing, seek external competitive and other funding, publish research findings and contribute to the successful supervision of research higher degree students, in order to meet and regularly exceed the University’s research performance expectations for Level B or Level C. Contribute to the development and maintenance of productive partnerships and effective relationships within the University and the discipline, relevant interdisciplinary domains, profession, industry and/or wider community at local and national levels. ­ What we’re looking for: Academic level B A PhD or equivalent in a relevant field. Demonstrated experience in leading and delivering high-quality teaching and learning in at least two of the following environments: bush, alpine, river, coastal, and / or rock. Demonstrated record of, and ongoing commitment to, research that has achieved national recognition and made worthwhile contributions to the field of Outdoor and Environmental Education, demonstrated by a record of quality publications, presentations at conferences and preferably success in securing external competitive and other funding. Demonstrated experience in delivering and supporting high-quality University level teaching and learning in Outdoor & Environmental Education Experience designing, developing or contributing to curriculum and assessment aligned with learning outcomes A record of contributing to building and maintaining effective and productive links locally and nationally with the discipline, profession, industry and wider community. Academic level C A PhD or equivalent in a relevant field. Demonstrated experience in leading and delivering high-quality teaching and learning at least two of bush, alpine, river, coastal, and / or rock environments A strong record in, and continuing commitment to, research that has achieved national and preferably international recognition and made notable contributions to the field of Outdoor and Environmental Education, demonstrated by a record of high-quality publications, presentations at conferences and success in securing external competitive and other funding. A demonstrated record of successful HDR supervision and research leadership, including contribution to research capacity building. Demonstrated experience in delivering and supporting high-quality University-level teaching and learning in Outdoor & Environmental Education Demonstrated experience designing or contributing to curriculum and assessment aligned with learning outcomes A record of contributing to building and maintaining effective and productive links locally and nationally with the discipline, profession, industry and wider community. Salary details Academic Level B and will have a total remuneration package of up to $155,885 comprising base salary within the range of $114,766 to $133,235 plus 17% superannuation. Academic Level C and will have a total remuneration package of up to $184,076 comprising base salary within the range of $138,536 to $157,330 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply To apply online, please provide the following supporting documentation: Resume Cover letter outlining your suitability and motivation for the role Your responses to the Role Specific Skills, Knowledge and Experience from the Position Description below For further information about this position, please contact Marcus Morse, Associate Professor in Outdoor and Environmental Education, marcus.morse@utas.edu.au Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description Below for full details. Position Description - 50417 - Lecturer in Outdoor and Environmental Education.pdf Position Description - 50417 - Senior Lecturer in Outdoor and Environmental Education.pdf Applications close Sunday, 4 October 2026, 11.55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of Back to job search Content missing Recommended Jobs Executive Director The Underwood Institute for Education Hobart, TAS. Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS Management Lead the Underwood Institute for Education to drive educational impact, partnership and system transformation across Tasmania. Learning & Research Librarian Hobart, TAS. Launceston, TAS Information Technology, Library Make a meaningful impact by empowering students, staff and researchers with inclusive learning and research support that enhances their information literacy and academic success. Senior Lecturer in Nursing Hobart, TAS. Launceston, TAS Teaching Intensive Share your nursing expertise, inspire the next generation and help shape the future of Tasmania’s nursing workforce Content missing © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
