    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/jobs/lecturer-senior-lecturer-in-education-hobart-tas-australia-launceston-burnie": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Education",
      "description": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Education - Hobart, TAS, Australia - Launceston, TAS, Australia - Burnie, TAS, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 0:00 Loaded : 0% Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 0:00 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles captions and subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Education 504190 Burnie, TAS Hobart, TAS Launceston, TAS Full time Closing on: 4 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Initial Teacher Education with expertise in Cognitive Science, Psychology and the Science of Learning Enjoy flexible working arrangements, generous superannuation and extensive leave provisions Full time, Ongoing role located in Hobart, Launceston or Burnie. Flexible work arrangements available About the opportunity Shape tomorrow's teachers through the science of learning. The School of Education is seeking passionate and innovative educators to join our team as either a Lecturer or Senior Lecturer in Education. Working within Initial Teacher Education, you will contribute to teaching, research and engagement activities with a focus on cognitive science, educational psychology and evidence-based teaching practices. Whether you are an emerging academic building your research profile or an established scholar with a record of academic leadership, this is an opportunity to influence how future teachers learn, teach and make a lasting impact in classrooms and communities. What you’ll do: Shape the next generation of teachers through high-quality teaching and mentorship. Deliver engaging learning experiences informed by cognitive science and evidence-based practice. Contribute to research that advances understanding of how students learn. Build strong partnerships with schools, communities and the broader education sector. Supervise and support research students. Collaborate with colleagues to drive excellence in teacher education. About you: Lecturer (Level B) Emerging or established teaching and research profile in education, cognitive science, psychology or a related field. Demonstrated capacity to contribute to research and teaching excellence. Interest in building research impact, grant success and academic leadership. S enior Lecturer (Level C) Established teaching and research profile with a record of academic leadership. Demonstrated success in research funding and supervision of higher degree research students. Capacity to teach across cognitive science and broader areas of teacher education. National, and ideally international, recognition in the field. Salary details Appointment to this role will be at Academic Level B or C and will have a total remuneration package of up to $184,076 comprising base salary within the range of $114,766 to $157,330 plus 17% superannuation. Relocation support may be available to the successful candidate, helping make a move to Tasmania as seamless as possible. How to Apply To apply online, please provide the following supporting documentation: Resume Cover letter outlining your suitability and motivation for the role Your responses to the success criteria from the Position Description below For further information about this position, please contact Professor Robyn Cox, Professor in Education, Robyn.Cox@utas.edu.au Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description Below for full details. Position Description - 504190 - Lecturer in Education.pdf Position Description - 504190 - Senior Lecturer in Education.pdf Applications close Sunday, 4 October 2026, 11.55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Back to job search Recommended Jobs Executive Director The Underwood Institute for Education Hobart, TAS. Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS Management Lead the Underwood Institute for Education to drive educational impact, partnership and system transformation across Tasmania. Learning & Research Librarian Hobart, TAS. Launceston, TAS Information Technology, Library Make a meaningful impact by empowering students, staff and researchers with inclusive learning and research support that enhances their information literacy and academic success. Senior Lecturer in Nursing Hobart, TAS. Launceston, TAS Teaching Intensive Share your nursing expertise, inspire the next generation and help shape the future of Tasmania’s nursing workforce © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
